  "description": "CR 708.2 a face-down copy of Silent Arbiter no longer bounds the attack",
  "note": "Silent Arbiter's attack bound is one of CR 613.11's rule-affecting families, read off the copiable values. alice's Clone copies her Silent Arbiter and bob's Murder destroys the printed one, since the bound is global and an Arbiter left standing would hold alice to one attacker whatever the Clone is. bob's Cyber Conversion (\"Turn target creature face down. It's a 2/2 Cyberman artifact creature\") turns the copy face down, so it has no abilities (CR 708.2) and both Goblin Pikers attack; one alone attacks too. Cyber Conversion names one creature, so the Pikers stay face up. The control leg, the same board without the Conversion, refuses the two-Piker declaration and takes the one-Piker one, so the refusal is the bound (CR 707.2a) rather than summoning sickness, a tap or a missing defender.",
